<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Waterford Wedgwood H1 pretax rises 28 pct.</title>
<headline>Waterford Wedgwood H1 pretax rises 28 pct.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-09-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>			   (million punts unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		1.08		   vs 0.82</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 0.30		   vs 0.25</p>
<p> Pretax profit	    9.5		    vs 7.4</p>
<p> Turnover		   163.2		  vs 150.9</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts were forecasting pre-tax profits of around 9.5 million Irish pounds.  </p>
<p> Operating profit	 11.4		   vs 10.1</p>
<p> Interest paid	    1.9		    vs 2.7</p>
<p> Tax charge		 1.7		    vs 1.6</p>
<p> Net taxed		  7.8		    vs 5.8</p>
<p> Retained profit	  5.6		    vs 3.9</p>
<p> Pay date		   Nov 29</p>
<p> Div registration date  Oct 22</p>
<p>NOTE - Crystal, fine china and tableware group Waterford Wedgwood Plc said on Wednesday that it had seen significant growth in the U.S., Japan and Ireland and that both its Waterford and Wedgwood brands performed strongly.  </p>
<p>The group said net debt at June 30 amounted to 56.9 million Irish pounds against 54.7 million last year. This represented a gearing level of 37 percent, down from 41 percent in 1995.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
</text>
